I have everything needed. Here is my report.

## Summary

The POST /owners pipeline is defined in OfficeFloor YAML and implemented as a chain of small Java "function" classes. Registration date is defaulted in `BuildOwner`, the membership number is built in `OwnerMapper` (using a year segment from the registration date), and the daily create-limit lives in `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`.

## 1. Owner creation / registration pipeline

Pipeline definition (POST /api/owners), `next:` chains the steps in order:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

Order: `build` -> `ensureUniqueTelephone` -> `ensureUniqueHousehold` -> `assignHousehold` -> `assignCustomerCode` -> `assignNamesakeCount` -> `ensureCityCapacity` -> `ensureDailyOwnerLimit` -> `save` -> `respond`. Authorization requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.

Corresponding Java function classes (all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):
- `BuildOwner.java` (validation, normalization, registrationDate default)
- `EnsureUniqueTelephone.java`, `EnsureUniqueHousehold.java`, `AssignHousehold.java`
- `AssignCustomerCode.java` (customer code)
- `AssignNamesakeCount.java`, `EnsureCityCapacity.java`
- `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit.java` (daily limit)
- `SaveOwner.java`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`
- Helpers: `Addresses.java`, `Telephones.java`, `OwnerEmails.java`

Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (fields `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, `namesakeCount`, `householdId`). Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`. Schema column `registration_date DATE` in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql:39` (also postgres/hsqldb/mysql schema.sql).

## 2. registrationDate set/default

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java` — the request value (if supplied and mapped) is kept, otherwise defaulted to the server's current date:

```java
